{"availability":"available","full":"ektogamat/r3f-webgpu-perf","name":"r3f-webgpu-perf","description":"r3f-webgpu-perf is a lightweight performance monitoring tool for React Three Fiber applications running on WebGPU. It provides real-time insights into frame timing, GPU workload, memory usage, draw calls, geometries, textures, and other rendering metrics through a modern, customizable interface designed for developers and technical artists.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":85,"forks":2,"created":"2026-06-08T20:18:45Z","updated":"2026-06-09T01:08:34Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://r3f-webgpu-perf.vercel.app/","topics":["performance-monitoring","r3f-perf","threejs"],"demo":"https://r3f-webgpu-perf.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:16.935Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:16.935Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:16.935Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T16:06:16.935Z","stars":85,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Easily monitor the performance of your @react-three/fiber application — built for React Three Fiber 8+ and designed to work with both WebGPU and WebGL renderers (including WebGPU setups where gl.info may be unavailable)."],"features":["WebGPU & WebGL — drop into any R3F Canvas; stats are collected from gl.info on WebGL or via scene traversal on WebGPU.","Light & dark mode — toggle the theme with the sun/moon button so the panel stays readable over bright or dark scenes.","Compact or expanded — click the chevron to expand the panel and reveal scene breakdown: draw calls, triangles, geometries, textures, lines, and points.","Minimize to a dot — hide the full panel with the eye button; it collapses to a small dot in the corner so it does not obstruct the viewport. Click the dot to bring it back.","FPS gauge, live graph & VRAM — circular gauge (cycles FPS → GPU → CPU), real-time graph, and optional VRAM estimate ba